dan simmons wrote the first book in the  Hyperion cantos in 1989 in this series  he followed in the footsteps of classic  science-fiction writers like Frank  Herbert and Isaac Asimov  since its release Hyperion has come to  be known as one of the essential  science-fiction books to come out of the  past three decades the series which  contains four books is set among the  stars within the hegemony of man  [Music]  the hegemony of man was the name given  to the political and cultural entity  which came to be after the event known  as the Hegira before the existence of  the hegemony the cradle of humanity  Earth had been destroyed by the event  afterward referred to as the big mistake  it was said to be a catastrophic  occurrence that caused the earth to be  consumed from the inside out  by a man created black hole over the  course of 100 years as the planet was  annihilated from within the Hegira began  the mass diaspora of humankind from the  planet earth and into the Stars the  results of the Hegira man's great exodus  from the planet Earth was the hegemony  which eventually would connect over 150  billion human beings inhabiting 200  planets there are also about 200 planets  considered protectorate of the hegemony  which were only reachable through  traditional means of space travel  these outback worlds were not connected  by far castor or fat line this means  that in traveling to these worlds time  debt is accumulated for instance two  weeks traveling at near light speed  would equate to about one standard year  relative to those outside of the ship  the planet Hyperion was one of such  worlds the planet Hyperion stood out for  several reasons it was the location of  the mysterious time tombs which had  appeared on the world at some point they  had been sent backward in time from some  point in the future another reason was  that Hyperion was the place where the  Shrike resided a deadly being which had  appeared on the planet at the same time  as the tombs the Church of the final  atonement or Shrike Church built a  temple on the world the strike was their  avatar their Lord of pain hundreds of  thousands of believers from throughout  the hegemony made the pilgrimage to the  strike temple Hyperion was also one of  the hegemonies nine labyrinthine worlds  these worlds each contain strange  complex underground tunnels it is  speculated that they  had been created by some ancient long  gone race referred to in the series as  the builders the hegemony of man's  government consisted of a bicameral  legislature ruled by the Senate the  Senate CEO who was essentially a  president and the whole thing the public  forum which could be accessed by any  member of the hegemony through calm logs  neural implants through which citizens  of the hegemony could be given  information about the state of the  Empire the all thing had evolved a  consciousness of its own through the all  thing citizens were able to vote on a  hundred different laws per day if they  chose the all thing was maintained by  artificial intelligence systems and was  dependent on fat line and far caster  technology the hegemonies armed forces  was collectively known as force many of  the soldiers were trained at the Olympus  command school which was built on a dead  volcano on the surface of the planet  Mars which was the first planet to be  colonized during the Hegira after the  big mistake force contained four  branches a marine force a space force a  Navy force and a ground force the  headquarters of force was located on Tau  Ceti Center a planet less than 12  light-years from old Earth's solar  system Tau Ceti center was the central  world of inhabited space and the capital  of the hegemony tens of billions of  humans lived there on the surface and  among the ring of habitats and cities in  orbit above the planet Tau Ceti Center  was also the center of the hegemony of  man's datum plane web mega sphere the  datum plane was the aggregate of all  real-time networks generated by computer  and AI the web mega sphere was one of  the two main data spheres within it the  other one was the Technic or matrix by  communicating through members of its AI  council the Technic or maintain an  advisory position within the hegemony  making predictions for the government  the techno core and the hegemony  government sustained a cooperative  relationship though the techno core had  a distant :  indicative of its inhuman nature for the  hegemony the techno core also created  many different technologies most notably  far casters and fat line technology  beyond the grip of the hegemony are the  ouster z' they were a society of humans  spread throughout the galaxy who  colonized the outer edges of human space  they had begun to set themselves apart  from the rest of humankind during the  beginning days of the Hegira in the four  books of the Hyperion cantos the ouster  remained the enemy of the hegemony and  later packs throughout the series much  about the actual nature of the ouster z'  is revealed  dan simmons provides in the Hyperion  cantos a strange and mysterious and  pretty scary universe I love the fact  that there are mysteries like what the  techno core is really up to or where the  time tooms came from or what exactly is  the purpose of these labyrinthine worlds  and who exactly were these ancient  builders and do they still exist  somewhere Dan Simmons is able to make  his Universe feel large and complex and  even convoluted at times without it  becoming overwhelming and without making  it feel like a non-stop barrage of names  and places that don't seem real the  hegemony of man controlled the majority  of the worlds that humankind had  inhabited though the citizens through  connection with the all thing could  participate in democracy the hegemony  was essentially a dictatorship led by  senators from various worlds many  planets had been forced into the  hegemony and no planet was permitted to  leave those who resisted would risk  being slaughtered by the military arm of  the hegemony which as I mentioned was  called force though the hegemony of  mankind marked a great achievement for  Humanity even away from the planet Earth  humans faced great struggles and  oppression  the hegemony of man perhaps like all  empires was destined one day to fall  thank you guys so much for watching if  you liked the video and want to see more  content make sure you like and subscribe  and if you want to support this channel  click the patreon link in the  description also check out the ideas of  Ice and Fire subreddit and follow me on  Twitter all of my links are in the  description
 

